@startuml pvp_kill_2c_drop
' =====================================================================
'  PvP kill - Diagrama 2c: parte 3 de GameMap::attack: DROP DE ORO E ITEMS, ARMADO DEL RESULT
'
'  Tercera parte de GameMap::attack: como J2 murio (target->is_dead()),
'  se spawnea el oro dropeado y caen TODOS sus items (incluidos casco y
'  armadura). Se construye el AttackResult que vuelve al GameLoop.
'
'  Situacion en docs/pvp_kill_escenario.md.
' =====================================================================
title PvP kill (2c) - Muerte de J2: drop de oro e items y AttackResult

participant "map:GameMap" as map
participant "j2:Player" as j2
participant "def:DefenseSet" as def
participant "inv:Inventory" as inv
participant "world:ZoneWorld" as world
participant "j1:Player" as j1
participant "loop:GameLoop" as loop

note over map
  Viene del Diagrama 2b con outcome: DamageOutcome
  (damage=160, gold_drop=drop, level_up).
end note
activate map

map -> j2 : is_dead(): bool
j2 --> map : true

== Drop de oro ==
map -> world : spawn_gold(x: int, y: int, amount=outcome.gold_drop: int): void
activate world
world --> map
deactivate world

== Drop de TODO el inventario (incluye casco y armadura) ==
map -> j2 : drop_inventory(): vector<unique_ptr<Item>>
activate j2
j2 -> def : clear(): void
note right of def
  El DefenseSet solo referenciaba casco/armadura;
  el dueno real es el Inventory.
end note
j2 -> inv : drop_all(): vector<unique_ptr<Item>>
activate inv
inv --> j2 : items   (Casco de hierro, Armadura de cuero, Arco compuesto, ...)
deactivate inv
j2 --> map : dropped: vector<unique_ptr<Item>>
deactivate j2

map -> world : scatter_items(center_x=x: int, center_y=y: int,\n  items: vector<unique_ptr<Item>>, players_here: vector<Player*>&): void
activate world
world --> map
deactivate world

== Armado del resultado ==
map -> j1 : get_level(): int
j1 --> map : level   (nuevo nivel si outcome.level_up == true)

map --> loop : AttackResult{ hit=true, entity_died=true,\n  target_is_player=true, entity_name="J2",\n  damage=160, target_x, target_y, dodged=false, level }
deactivate map

note over loop
  Con el AttackResult, handle_attack arma los GameMsg para el
  atacante J1 y para la victima J2 => Diagramas 3a / 3b.
end note

@enduml
